  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "An acidified manganate solution undergoes disproportionation reaction. The spin-only magnetic moment value of the product having manganese in higher oxidation state is____B.M. (Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>As we can see in this reaction oxidised product of reaction is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;which has no unpaired electrons. So, magnetic moment will be zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>=</mo></math> no. of unpaired electrons is &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&#39;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
